{
    "name": "E2E IDeaS - make api call",
    "description": "Sends one inventory date through Make API Call with its own ReplyTo header and checks that IDeaS accepted it.",
    "notes": {
        "bde19133-59c2-443d-87e0-51b622902d98": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 208,
            "width": 880,
            "height": 288,
            "content": "## Never run\n\nWritten from the IDeaS documentation; it has only passed `appmixer e2e validate`. See README.md in this folder.\n\n## Test data assumptions\n\n- The body names `TESTCLIENT` / `TESTHOTELCODE` (the documentation's sample codes). Replace them with the codes of the test property.\n- The `ReplyTo` header is required by IDeaS (the request is refused without it), so the assert on the status code also shows that the header reached IDeaS. It points at this connector's reply route with a token that is not valid: IDeaS's result is answered 404 and goes nowhere. Make API Call never receives a result; the Send components do."
        }
    },
